        'rawContent': '{{Aircraft Information|\n|name = XB-1 (Imperial Experimental Airframe)\n|image = \n|caption = XB-1 (Imperial Experimental Airframe)\n|mission_profile = XX\n|crew = XX\n|first_flight = \n|manufacturer = XX\n|operator = XX\n|length = x meters\n|wingspan = x meters\n|height = x meters\n|powerplant = XX\n|propulsion = XX x XX Engines <br/> Maximum Acceleration: XX KPH/s <br/> Maximum Airspeed: XX <br/> Maximum Velocity: XX 0.1xC\n|max_airspeed = \n|fixed_weapons = XX\n|armor = XX <br/> XX\n|shields = \n}}\n\nGeneral Characteristics\r\n*Designation: XX\r\n*Length: x meters\r\n*Width: x meters\r\n*Height: x meters\r\n*Power: XX\r\n*Propulsion: XX x XX Engines\r\n**Maximum Acceleration: XX KPH/s\r\n**Maximum Airspeed: XX\r\n**Maximum Velocity: XX 0.1xC\r\n*Operation Time: XX Hours\r\n*Crew: XX\r\n*Communications System: XX\r\n*Targeting and Tracking System: XX\r\n*Processing System: XX\r\n*Armament: \r\n**XX\r\n*Defenses: \r\n**XX\r\n**XX\r\n*Operators:\r\n**XX\r\n*Number built: XX\r\n*Unit cost: XX\r\n*Manufacturer: XX\r\n\r\nThe XB-1 was the first Imperial bomber, based off the F-4 airframe. It was built with much larger fuel tanks for the ion engine to handle the significantly greater mass of the Anti-Warship Torpedoes (AWT). The design was also stripped of its guns, and the heat shielding plates necessary for an atmospheric reentry. The YB-1 was used in attack runs on asteroids with F-4s escorting and F-4s "defending" the target. The YB-1 was put into extremely limited production, but cancelled with only 30 delivered due to fuel problems limiting the range of the bomber too much.\r\n\r\n[[Category:Bombers]]'
